  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday morning through next Friday)\nIssued at 243 PM EDT Sat Oct 10 2026\n\nNo changes were made to the longterm forecast.\n\nThe long term picks up after the remnants of Isaias are not but a \nmemory. Dry air will settle in across the southeast and bring back a \nlittle bit of summer on the backside. Highs in the mid to upper 80s \nare expected as high pressure keeps winds out of the west. Drier \nconditions will start off the long term, but as the high slowly \nmeanders to the east, we'll start to see a moisture return by the \nmiddle part of the work week brining afternoon heat index values \nback into the 90s. \n\nExpect overnight lows to be comfortably in the 50s and 60s for much \nof the area with winds becoming light and variable during the \novernight hours. By next weekend, some of the model runs are \nbeginning to indicate the possibility for a strong cold front to \npush down from the north that will bring fall back into the region. \nBut for the meantime, enjoy a little bit more late summer and plenty \nof sunshine.",
